WEBVTT

00:18.727 --> 00:21.146
BOSS

00:59.476 --> 01:02.854
BLOODHOUNDS

01:02.937 --> 01:05.857
Fuck. This is insane.

01:20.163 --> 01:21.081
Mr. Bae.

01:21.164 --> 01:23.541
Get me the address of the woman
who runs the café.

01:23.625 --> 01:25.126
These shitheads are ready to fight.

01:25.960 --> 01:27.003
You fuckers.

01:28.505 --> 01:30.131
You sons of bitches!

01:37.764 --> 01:38.598
Damn it!

01:52.779 --> 01:54.155
Come here, you son of a bitch!

01:55.657 --> 01:57.450
Damn it, you fuckers!

02:08.044 --> 02:09.170
Damn it!

02:12.006 --> 02:12.924
You bastard!

02:20.890 --> 02:23.017
- Go at him all at once!
- You bastard.

02:42.245 --> 02:43.663
Fuck!

02:47.417 --> 02:48.585
You sons of bitches!

02:49.169 --> 02:50.253
Come here!

02:53.214 --> 02:54.132
This bastard!

03:08.938 --> 03:10.273
Motherfucker!

03:14.861 --> 03:15.778
Fuck him up!

03:18.072 --> 03:19.365
You fucker!

03:27.790 --> 03:28.625
Hey, you punk!

03:31.127 --> 03:31.961
You bastard!

03:37.926 --> 03:39.344
Damn it.

03:53.316 --> 03:54.943
- You sons of bitches!
- You bastard!

04:18.591 --> 04:19.425
Damn it!

04:34.565 --> 04:35.525
Son of a…

04:37.652 --> 04:38.987
Get over here!

04:39.070 --> 04:40.113
Damn it!

04:54.711 --> 04:56.129
Get up! Move!

05:21.404 --> 05:23.072
- Let's go, Gun-woo.
- Okay.

05:23.781 --> 05:25.116
- Let's go!
- Right.

05:29.120 --> 05:30.580
Thanks for coming, Hyeon-ju.

05:31.539 --> 05:32.707
I'm sorry I came late.

05:33.541 --> 05:35.043
You saved us quite a beating.

05:37.253 --> 05:38.212
Damn, that hurts.

05:52.268 --> 05:53.895
Is that you, Gun-woo?

06:05.948 --> 06:07.241
Gun-woo?

06:22.799 --> 06:24.008
Hey, it's all right.

06:47.865 --> 06:49.450
- Hurry up and move.
- Yes, sir.

06:56.290 --> 06:57.125
Hey.

07:04.048 --> 07:06.342
Who the fuck is he?

07:08.428 --> 07:10.263
This is fucking annoying.

07:27.405 --> 07:28.406
Fuck.

07:50.303 --> 07:51.137
Hold on.

08:05.026 --> 08:06.277
Fuck!

08:38.100 --> 08:39.810
Who the fuck are you?

08:53.824 --> 08:56.035
Shut your mouth, you bastard.

09:01.040 --> 09:03.209
Get up!

09:28.276 --> 09:29.944
God, stop!

09:52.717 --> 09:53.843
Look at that.

09:57.972 --> 09:58.931
Hey.

09:59.890 --> 10:01.017
Who the hell are you?

10:01.767 --> 10:02.935
- Sorry, sir.
- Stop.

10:04.103 --> 10:05.813
I asked you a fucking question.

10:17.116 --> 10:18.159
Sleep tight.

10:30.546 --> 10:31.589
What is this?

10:32.173 --> 10:33.633
When did I get hit like this?

10:44.018 --> 10:45.603
MY LOVELY MOM

10:47.688 --> 10:48.648
Yes, Mom.

10:48.731 --> 10:49.732
Gun-woo.

10:51.484 --> 10:53.736
Mom? What happened? Why are you crying?

10:55.488 --> 10:56.989
Someone wants to talk to you.

11:01.160 --> 11:02.370
Where are you guys?

11:28.104 --> 11:29.313
Gun-woo.

11:33.192 --> 11:35.194
Mom, what happened to your forehead?

11:36.195 --> 11:37.488
It's all right.

11:38.781 --> 11:40.658
I just bumped my head on the ground.

11:44.245 --> 11:45.079
Your face…

11:49.083 --> 11:51.419
Woo-jin, what happened to your face?

11:52.002 --> 11:54.213
Well, it's just a scratch.

11:55.047 --> 11:57.842
Mr. Choi's been worried sick
waiting for you.

11:57.925 --> 11:59.301
Let's go down.

11:59.927 --> 12:00.845
- Okay.
- Okay.

12:04.265 --> 12:05.349
I'll be back.

12:09.228 --> 12:10.563
Everyone, sit down!

12:18.237 --> 12:20.740
I'm sure you're all tired,
so I'll keep this short.

12:23.993 --> 12:25.411
When I got your call,

12:26.287 --> 12:28.372
it felt like the end of the world for me.

12:30.249 --> 12:31.917
You're my family.

12:33.502 --> 12:36.547
I was so afraid that I might lose you.

12:37.423 --> 12:39.091
I'll no longer condone you getting hurt.

12:39.925 --> 12:41.969
Let the adults handle the rest.

12:42.720 --> 12:45.097
- I also want to help.
- Gun-woo.

12:45.681 --> 12:49.602
This isn't a match
where someone wins or loses.

12:50.686 --> 12:53.272
This is a war that will only end
once someone's dead.

12:57.777 --> 12:58.903
You two go upstairs.

13:10.289 --> 13:11.332
I'm sorry.

13:11.415 --> 13:13.459
Promise me
you'll never get involved again!

13:14.335 --> 13:15.169
Okay.

13:15.920 --> 13:18.881
They know where Gun-woo lives,
so it's dangerous to go there.

13:19.465 --> 13:21.634
Take Gun-woo's mother
to the orphanage tomorrow.

13:21.717 --> 13:23.803
It'll be much safer for her to stay there.

13:25.638 --> 13:26.472
Okay.

13:27.807 --> 13:28.849
Good night.

13:37.942 --> 13:39.902
Yang-jung, what do we do now?

13:42.738 --> 13:43.864
I'll put an end to this.

13:46.158 --> 13:49.119
We should've taken care of this
a long time ago.

13:50.246 --> 13:51.831
Can you get Myeong-gil?

13:51.914 --> 13:54.375
I'll team up
with Du-yeong starting tomorrow.

13:55.376 --> 13:56.544
I'll pick them off.

13:56.627 --> 13:58.504
Let's eat with Du-yeong.

13:58.587 --> 13:59.922
Mr. Oh.

14:00.422 --> 14:02.800
Please look into Myeong-gil's men.

14:02.883 --> 14:03.759
Yes, sir.

15:33.557 --> 15:36.185
Director, you're here
so early in the morning.

15:36.268 --> 15:38.437
I had to come for you, Mr. Kim.

15:39.730 --> 15:41.315
I operated on them myself.

15:41.398 --> 15:42.900
I see. Thank you.

15:42.983 --> 15:46.862
One of them had both
of his Achilles tendons cut with a knife.

15:47.446 --> 15:51.033
The other had all of the tendons
in his shoulders severed.

16:04.588 --> 16:05.589
He had short hair

16:06.757 --> 16:08.342
and slanted eyes.

16:09.760 --> 16:11.220
He was very quick on his feet.

16:11.929 --> 16:14.181
And his knife skills were superb.

16:18.560 --> 16:19.395
And?

16:19.478 --> 16:20.688
Yes, well…

16:22.106 --> 16:23.941
It appeared to be a sashimi knife.

16:27.403 --> 16:28.237
Fuck.

16:33.617 --> 16:35.744
Tell Beom to get to the office by 1 p.m.

16:35.828 --> 16:37.788
- Let's have a meeting.
- Yes, sir.

16:38.622 --> 16:40.040
Things just got interesting.

16:50.217 --> 16:52.177
- Finish this up.
- Okay.

16:54.555 --> 16:56.223
- Sir.
- Yes?

16:58.767 --> 16:59.810
I'll go with you.

17:01.353 --> 17:02.396
Stay.

17:03.522 --> 17:04.898
I want to help, sir.

17:04.982 --> 17:06.025
Min-dong.

17:07.651 --> 17:09.194
I'll take care of it myself.

17:10.070 --> 17:11.822
You just live your life.

17:12.489 --> 17:15.367
Sir, I want to join you!

17:15.451 --> 17:16.410
Hey.

17:17.119 --> 17:20.372
If the restaurant is in ruins
by the time I get back,

17:20.456 --> 17:21.290
what will you do?

17:22.499 --> 17:24.752
Protect the store.
That's how you can help me.

17:25.419 --> 17:26.336
But still--

17:30.007 --> 17:30.841
Watch the store.

18:17.930 --> 18:19.056
Hwang Yang-jung!

18:19.640 --> 18:20.808
It's been so long.

18:20.891 --> 18:22.559
Why haven't you been in touch?

18:22.643 --> 18:24.269
I was busy making a living.

18:24.812 --> 18:26.897
How did your handsome face get so old?

18:26.980 --> 18:28.774
Making an honest living isn't easy.

18:28.857 --> 18:29.983
Right?

18:30.067 --> 18:31.819
It's so hard. Isn't it?

18:34.196 --> 18:35.572
- Man, it's been so long.
- Yes.

18:36.573 --> 18:39.576
I called Su-cheol and Min-su
to have them look into it.

18:40.077 --> 18:41.537
This is pretty big.

18:42.621 --> 18:45.958
They aren't your average loan sharks.
Something's off about them.

18:47.584 --> 18:48.502
Thank you.

18:48.585 --> 18:49.419
Thanks.

18:54.174 --> 18:55.843
A friend in Yeouido heard

18:56.426 --> 18:59.847
that Iil Group purchased
an unfinished hotel building in Gangnam.

19:00.514 --> 19:03.100
They got their money
from a company called Smile Capital.

19:03.183 --> 19:04.560
Kim Myeong-gil's company.

19:04.643 --> 19:06.353
Yeah,

19:07.020 --> 19:10.315
but why would a chaebol borrow money
from Kim Myeong-gil? I don't get it.

19:12.025 --> 19:14.236
Kim Myeong-gil probably
tricked them into it.

19:15.612 --> 19:17.239
- Let's do some digging.
- Okay.

19:19.950 --> 19:21.869
We're finally avenging our boys.

19:23.912 --> 19:24.872
Let's end this.

19:25.664 --> 19:27.166
Mr. Choi gave us his approval.

19:30.002 --> 19:30.836
Okay.

19:31.670 --> 19:36.300
Back in the day, President Choi
had five knifers working for him.

19:36.383 --> 19:39.928
At the time, President Choi
lent money to corporations,

19:40.012 --> 19:42.431
so he had 10 billion won
or more in uncollected money.

19:42.514 --> 19:44.558
But places like
construction companies had gangs

19:45.309 --> 19:47.186
that looked out for them.

19:47.269 --> 19:49.229
That's when these guys would go.

19:49.730 --> 19:53.317
They'd go out
and obliterate an entire gang in a day.

19:53.400 --> 19:57.654
Back then, even the big gangs were
terrified of President Choi's knifers.

19:59.656 --> 20:02.409
After I got President Choi out of the way,

20:03.660 --> 20:05.495
the first thing I did with Beom

20:05.996 --> 20:07.414
was get rid of his knifers.

20:07.497 --> 20:08.665
Do you know why?

20:09.833 --> 20:10.751
No, sir.

20:11.752 --> 20:14.838
Because I was scared as shit too. Fuck.

20:17.049 --> 20:18.800
Was it just you two?

20:18.884 --> 20:23.347
We sent two gangs, one from Sindang-dong
and one from Yeongdeungpo, as a unit.

20:23.430 --> 20:26.350
It was only possible
because they weren't together at the time.

20:26.433 --> 20:28.602
Otherwise, it would have been impossible.

20:28.685 --> 20:30.520
Whoa. That's amazing, sir.

20:30.604 --> 20:32.022
But in the end,

20:33.023 --> 20:35.525
I couldn't get rid of
the two most important ones.

20:36.985 --> 20:40.113
Lee Du-yeong and Hwang Yang-jung.

20:40.697 --> 20:43.742
President Choi's top lieutenants.

20:45.244 --> 20:50.207
I ran into Lee Du-yeong once
when I was President Choi's lackey.

20:50.290 --> 20:51.500
He's a handsome one.

20:53.001 --> 20:55.587
This one time,
a gang leader was stuck in traffic,

20:55.671 --> 20:58.090
so he had a smoke
with his window rolled down.

20:58.173 --> 21:00.968
When he heard a motorcycle approaching,
he turned his head.

21:01.051 --> 21:04.930
And Lee Du-yeong carved his face like this
with a sashimi knife and rode away.

21:05.013 --> 21:07.474
His mouth got fucking big,
flapping around like this.

21:07.557 --> 21:09.101
Shit, that's crazy.

21:11.103 --> 21:12.104
Who's Hwang Yang-jung?

21:12.187 --> 21:14.231
Well, they say…

21:15.774 --> 21:18.819
he crippled 20 gang members

21:18.902 --> 21:20.821
by severing their Achilles tendons.

21:20.904 --> 21:23.073
He fights with two knives

21:23.156 --> 21:25.534
and is rumored
to stab 100 times in one minute.

21:26.034 --> 21:27.327
Fucking crazy, huh?

21:30.622 --> 21:33.542
Right. Did you say
that three kids showed up?

21:33.625 --> 21:36.545
Yes, sir. A girl showed up halfway.

21:37.045 --> 21:40.215
I believe she's connected to
that bookstore I mentioned before.

21:43.427 --> 21:45.637
It makes sense if he owns the bookstore.

21:45.721 --> 21:49.725
That senile fuck must have crawled out
of the shadows to save his kids.

21:52.269 --> 21:54.104
Do you know how much President Choi has?

21:55.772 --> 21:59.776
I'd guess about 50 billion in cash.

22:01.028 --> 22:03.113
That would cover the money
we're short on the casino.

22:05.032 --> 22:08.744
Someone has to be looking out for us
up there. Don't you think?

22:11.455 --> 22:14.916
Jang-do and Beom. Stake out the place
and bring me everything.

22:20.047 --> 22:26.928
LOVE ORPHANAGE

22:33.310 --> 22:34.227
Aren't you coming?

22:35.103 --> 22:37.314
I don't want to go in. Make it quick.

22:38.315 --> 22:39.900
All right. We'll be right back.

22:42.319 --> 22:44.529
- Kids, this way.
- Look at this one.

22:44.613 --> 22:45.614
This way, please.

22:47.949 --> 22:50.202
It's a kid's room, so it's a bit small.

22:50.285 --> 22:52.996
But it'll be fine to stay in.
Take your time looking around.

22:53.080 --> 22:53.997
Thank you.

23:13.934 --> 23:16.686
Mom, how do you like this place?
Hey, it's Woo-jin.

23:16.770 --> 23:18.105
Hello, ma'am.

23:24.069 --> 23:25.987
A friend from elementary school

23:26.071 --> 23:29.616
works for one of Kim Myeong-gil's men,
so he was on the scene that day.

23:30.242 --> 23:32.494
From what I've heard, things got intense.

23:33.245 --> 23:34.996
They were waiting at the gas station.

23:35.080 --> 23:36.998
And as soon as the Iil Group heir came in,

23:37.082 --> 23:39.501
they locked him up,
beat him, and threatened him.

23:40.710 --> 23:44.423
They must be the only ones in Korea
that would do that to the chaebol.

23:44.506 --> 23:45.465
And?

23:45.549 --> 23:47.217
They got a video of the guy…

23:58.061 --> 24:01.148
This is Kim Jun-min,
the sales director at Smile Capital.

24:01.231 --> 24:02.858
He has six priors for fraud.

24:03.775 --> 24:05.861
Used car fraud,
credit card payment fraud, etc.

24:05.944 --> 24:07.988
You name it, he's done it.

24:08.071 --> 24:10.991
Apparently, he served
at Seoul Nambu Detention Center.

24:12.075 --> 24:14.953
Im Jang-do was a cadet
at the Police University

24:15.620 --> 24:18.039
until he got kicked out
for sexual harassment.

24:18.123 --> 24:21.460
He has no priors. He's Smile Capital's
head of strategic planning.

24:22.043 --> 24:23.128
That's unusual.

24:23.837 --> 24:26.965
Having a guy who knows
how the police operate

24:27.048 --> 24:29.509
would help them
avoid police investigations.

24:29.593 --> 24:30.719
So, it's these two?

24:31.219 --> 24:32.137
Yes.

24:32.846 --> 24:33.889
What about their addresses?

24:34.389 --> 24:35.891
I have one for this guy.

24:36.600 --> 24:38.101
He lives in Saseong-dong.

24:38.185 --> 24:40.020
We know his car and the plate number.

24:41.188 --> 24:42.522
We should get moving fast.

24:43.732 --> 24:45.275
They'll catch on soon.

24:45.358 --> 24:46.193
Yes.

24:46.860 --> 24:48.987
I'll take this one.

24:50.739 --> 24:53.992
- Tomorrow night?
- But how far should we go?

24:54.075 --> 24:56.536
What do you mean?
We should take them out for good.

24:59.748 --> 25:01.082
I'll take Kim Myeong-gil.

25:01.666 --> 25:03.001
He doesn't move alone.

25:03.919 --> 25:06.838
Everything about him isn't
what it seems. Go with Du-yeong.

25:08.757 --> 25:10.091
I'll just tail him.

25:12.052 --> 25:14.888
Wasn't there a burly one with Myeong-gil?

25:14.971 --> 25:16.014
Well, yes.

25:16.848 --> 25:19.601
The detective agency asked for more time.

25:20.685 --> 25:22.812
I'll look into it more.

25:23.355 --> 25:24.189
Who is he?

25:25.023 --> 25:28.109
The guy who threw me out the window
is as strong as an ox.

25:31.863 --> 25:35.116
Sir, what will you do
about the cash in the bookstore?

25:35.700 --> 25:36.952
We have to move it.

25:37.035 --> 25:38.787
He knows the location.

25:39.287 --> 25:41.748
Why don't we have the kids move the cash?

25:44.501 --> 25:48.505
The thing is, we don't have time
and are short on manpower.

25:50.423 --> 25:52.259
Those kids are no joke.

25:52.342 --> 25:55.136
- They mowed down 30 men.
- Did you see it happen?

25:55.220 --> 25:57.305
I went over, but they were on the ground.

25:57.806 --> 26:00.850
Thirty men between the three of them,
without using knives…

26:00.934 --> 26:02.686
They're not your average kids.

26:03.311 --> 26:06.940
Sir, it should be fine
if they move it early in the morning.

26:07.023 --> 26:08.567
Why don't you give them a chance?

26:09.150 --> 26:10.652
Hyeon-ju's a smart kid too.

26:17.659 --> 26:19.202
Okay, put it here.

26:20.912 --> 26:21.746
Here.

26:24.874 --> 26:25.834
This looks amazing.

26:28.712 --> 26:30.005
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

26:30.088 --> 26:31.590
- Thank you.
- Sure, hurry and eat.

26:32.340 --> 26:33.592
You first, Hyeon-ju.

26:34.926 --> 26:36.511
Okay, thank you.

26:44.769 --> 26:46.688
Did you use our kimchi to make this?

26:46.771 --> 26:47.772
Yes.

26:48.815 --> 26:51.693
It tastes totally different
from when I make it.

26:53.028 --> 26:54.696
It's easy. I'll teach you how.

26:56.531 --> 26:57.365
Okay.

27:02.621 --> 27:04.998
I wanted to ask something.

27:05.081 --> 27:09.836
Is the orphanage run by Mr. Choi?

27:10.587 --> 27:12.172
Well, yes.

27:12.255 --> 27:14.966
According to Grandpa,
he used to be very poor.

27:15.050 --> 27:18.053
His dream was to help those in need
if he made a lot of money.

27:18.136 --> 27:19.471
I see.

27:20.138 --> 27:22.891
Are you his granddaughter?

27:23.475 --> 27:28.104
No. I was placed in the orphanage
after my parents passed away.

27:28.188 --> 27:29.814
I see. I'm sorry.

27:30.482 --> 27:32.567
Jeez. I shouldn't have brought that up.

27:33.860 --> 27:34.944
No, not at all.

27:36.112 --> 27:36.946
I'm sorry.

27:39.741 --> 27:41.618
What kind of food do you enjoy, Hyeon-ju?

27:43.119 --> 27:43.953
Well,

27:45.413 --> 27:46.998
I like rolled omelets.

27:47.499 --> 27:49.376
I see. Have some of this.

27:50.627 --> 27:52.837
Oh! Where did all the rolled omelets go?

27:54.589 --> 27:57.842
You should have left some for Hyeon-ju.

28:03.181 --> 28:05.850
That's right. I wanted rolled omelets.

28:10.355 --> 28:11.481
Let me make more.

28:11.564 --> 28:12.565
No, that's all right.

28:12.649 --> 28:14.901
No, this won't take long. Wait a minute.

28:14.984 --> 28:16.903
Mom, make it big and thick.

28:16.986 --> 28:18.321
All right.

28:18.405 --> 28:19.614
A lot, please.

28:19.698 --> 28:21.783
All right. I'll make them huge.

28:24.285 --> 28:25.286
Hurry up and eat.

28:32.377 --> 28:35.547
THE DAY AFTER TOMORROW, GO TO
THE BOOKSTORE AND GET ALL THE CASH OUT

28:51.771 --> 28:53.773
KIM JUN-MIN

29:24.095 --> 29:24.929
Take it easy.

29:51.623 --> 29:53.208
- Did you pack everything?
- Yes.

30:25.990 --> 30:27.992
Fuck. This is scary.

32:30.156 --> 32:32.075
Start making the boxes.
I'll get the money.

32:32.158 --> 32:33.826
How will we move these to the car?

32:33.910 --> 32:34.994
We'll carry them.

32:35.078 --> 32:37.747
No, that would take too long.
Do you have any trolleys?

32:37.830 --> 32:40.458
Yes. In the storage room
downstairs on the left.

32:40.541 --> 32:42.460
Woo-jin and I will go get them.

32:42.543 --> 32:44.212
Arrange the money on the floor.

32:44.295 --> 32:45.338
- Right.
- Let's go.

33:56.659 --> 33:59.078
Hey, you're a tough one.

34:32.320 --> 34:33.321
What are you doing?

34:33.905 --> 34:35.281
Don't let him grab you.

34:35.364 --> 34:37.408
- Who is that?
- The guy I mentioned before.

34:38.076 --> 34:39.577
Fucking hell.

35:48.980 --> 35:50.606
Hit and duck faster.

35:50.690 --> 35:51.691
Okay.

36:33.482 --> 36:35.151
You little shit.

37:17.985 --> 37:18.861
Fuck.

37:29.580 --> 37:31.165
Hey, you fuck!

39:09.221 --> 39:11.182
Calm down. Stop, that's enough.

39:13.059 --> 39:14.852
That's enough.

39:17.021 --> 39:18.105
It's okay.

39:20.649 --> 39:21.609
It's all over.

39:22.443 --> 39:25.029
Everything's okay.

39:29.200 --> 39:30.993
- Let's tie him up.
- Right.

39:34.538 --> 39:36.540
- Let's find something to tie him with!
- Okay.

39:40.127 --> 39:42.213
- You go check out that side.
- Okay.

39:47.551 --> 39:48.552
Damn it.

39:54.642 --> 39:55.768
Woo-jin!

39:57.228 --> 39:58.145
Let's tie him.

40:01.565 --> 40:02.400
Wait.

40:04.610 --> 40:06.278
What the hell? What happened to you?

40:06.362 --> 40:07.613
I got into a fucking fight.

40:07.696 --> 40:08.572
Are you all right?

40:08.656 --> 40:10.491
It's gonna hurt like a bitch tomorrow.

40:10.991 --> 40:14.578
Why did you tie his hands to the front?
That's going to come off easily.

40:14.662 --> 40:16.122
Well, I don't think so.

40:16.205 --> 40:17.415
Should I tie it again?

40:17.498 --> 40:19.750
Hurry up and tie him.
Gun-woo, get the trolley.

40:19.834 --> 40:20.960
Okay.

40:22.086 --> 40:23.003
Hold his feet.

40:26.257 --> 40:27.967
All right. Let's go.

40:30.136 --> 40:31.470
- Our jackets.
- Damn it. Hurry.

40:31.554 --> 40:32.555
This one's expensive.

40:42.481 --> 40:44.191
I had him cuffed up here.

40:47.278 --> 40:49.280
He got away
because you cuffed him to a pipe.

40:50.030 --> 40:52.199
You should have cuffed him up properly.

40:52.283 --> 40:53.117
Damn it.

41:11.552 --> 41:12.720
IM JANG-DO

41:16.640 --> 41:17.641
What took you so long?

41:18.309 --> 41:20.227
We've run into a bit of a problem.

41:20.311 --> 41:21.145
And the money?

41:21.645 --> 41:23.898
Don't worry. The money's still there.

41:23.981 --> 41:25.524
Where are you off to?

41:25.608 --> 41:27.193
I can't get in touch with In-beom.

41:27.276 --> 41:29.737
My face and mouth are badly torn,

41:30.404 --> 41:31.614
so I'll drop by the ER

41:31.697 --> 41:33.407
before heading back to the scene.

41:33.491 --> 41:34.408
What do you mean?

41:34.909 --> 41:36.702
Clean up your mess before you go.

41:36.785 --> 41:38.204
Yes. You're right, sir.

41:38.287 --> 41:40.581
But my face is badly bleeding.

41:40.664 --> 41:42.374
My teeth are all loose, so I should--

41:42.458 --> 41:44.376
Hey, you fucking son of a bitch.

41:44.460 --> 41:47.421
Call Jung. Gather his men
and take them down now.

41:48.464 --> 41:51.884
I want their heads, got it?
Look at this fucker trying to play hooky.

41:51.967 --> 41:53.469
Fucking hell. Do you wish to die?

41:53.552 --> 41:57.223
Before I rip their heads off,
should I chop off yours first, asshole?

41:58.140 --> 41:59.225
I'll do as you wish,

42:00.184 --> 42:01.060
sir.

42:13.656 --> 42:14.698
Move!

42:16.784 --> 42:18.035
Hurry up and get in.

42:28.295 --> 42:29.296
Throw it!

42:44.895 --> 42:46.355
- Pop the trunk.
- All right.

42:47.314 --> 42:48.148
Push!

42:58.117 --> 42:59.493
Be careful.

42:59.577 --> 43:00.494
Hurry.

43:01.870 --> 43:02.871
Damn it.

43:05.457 --> 43:06.375
Okay, we're done.

43:06.458 --> 43:07.876
Fuck. We have to get the safe.

43:08.586 --> 43:09.837
Don't we have to leave now?

43:09.920 --> 43:10.879
Go up first.

43:10.963 --> 43:11.880
How much is there?

43:11.964 --> 43:13.465
Billions, at least.

43:14.049 --> 43:14.925
I'll help.

43:15.426 --> 43:17.386
- You go up first.
- Well…

43:17.469 --> 43:21.307
Hey, we have to get the billions.

43:21.390 --> 43:23.601
Get the car running and wait.
We'll be back fast.

43:24.101 --> 43:25.227
You have to hurry.

43:28.814 --> 43:31.233
- Woo-jin, there's a bag under the cabinet.
- Okay.

43:36.196 --> 43:37.740
Fuck! A gold bar?

43:37.823 --> 43:41.035
- Jeez. Get packing!
- Right.

43:46.415 --> 43:47.416
Dollars?

43:48.000 --> 43:49.793
Don't just sit there. Get packing.

43:50.461 --> 43:51.462
Got it.

44:20.699 --> 44:23.035
Damn. Someone took a beating.

44:23.744 --> 44:24.662
Are you all right?

44:27.623 --> 44:28.582
Follow me.

44:42.763 --> 44:44.056
Take it slow.

44:44.139 --> 44:45.516
Why is there so much money?

44:49.311 --> 44:51.063
Hurry up!

44:51.146 --> 44:53.107
These are so damn heavy!

44:58.737 --> 44:59.613
All right.

45:05.869 --> 45:06.704
Okay.

45:26.682 --> 45:27.850
Call Gun-woo.

45:31.937 --> 45:32.771
Yes, Woo-jin.

45:33.522 --> 45:34.982
Stay on my tail.

45:35.482 --> 45:36.316
Okay.

45:47.745 --> 45:48.871
Fuck!

45:51.165 --> 45:51.999
Damn it.

46:17.733 --> 46:19.443
Gun-woo, can you speed up?

46:19.526 --> 46:21.779
I think the car is weighed down right now.

46:21.862 --> 46:23.530
When I signal you, go ahead of me.

46:24.490 --> 46:25.449
All right. I'll try.

46:30.370 --> 46:31.705
Now, step on it!

46:41.173 --> 46:42.174
Fuck.

47:11.745 --> 47:12.913
Damn it.

47:22.005 --> 47:22.965
Hurry up and get in.

47:38.605 --> 47:39.982
They're coming. Go faster!

47:40.607 --> 47:42.025
The car is acting up!

47:56.081 --> 47:56.957
Fuck!

48:13.932 --> 48:15.309
Fuck.

48:15.934 --> 48:16.935
Damn it. Hold tight!

48:21.773 --> 48:22.733
Damn it!

48:22.816 --> 48:24.693
Woo-jin! Are you all right?

48:52.471 --> 48:53.889
Here we go!

49:09.988 --> 49:11.782
Push!

49:18.246 --> 49:20.749
More!

49:24.503 --> 49:25.504
Woo-jin!

49:30.926 --> 49:32.219
Push to the right!

49:36.264 --> 49:37.808
Push! More!

49:47.109 --> 49:48.610
Step on it!

49:52.739 --> 49:53.991
- Damn it.
- It stopped.

49:54.491 --> 49:55.409
Fuck!

49:56.243 --> 49:59.204
The car's done for. Get out.
We need to get the bags.

50:07.462 --> 50:08.380
Run!

50:12.884 --> 50:13.885
Run. Fast!

50:37.951 --> 50:38.785
Hey!

50:41.705 --> 50:42.706
Run faster!
